From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:58:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/44] qwen27: dump per-layer residuals from the real-weight
 gate

A port needs the first layer whose residual leaves the reference, not just a
token mismatch. Stages.begin now answers the tap hook at embedding_tap (1000),
which no layer index collides with, so a dump carries the rows layer 0 starts
from; tf-qwen27-run takes --dump-taps L0,L1,... and --dump PATH and writes each
tapped plane as raw bf16 with a 16-byte header of planes, rows, width, capacity.

Measured with it on SenseNova-Loop-9B: the packed embedding matches the
reference (max 0.0133, cos 0.99395, i.e. the 4-bit group step) and layer 0, a
Gated-DeltaNet layer, is the first divergence (delta cos 0.857 with rms 1.65x
the reference). The converter also ships A_log in bf16 to match the decay
kernel's declared dtype.
---
 tools/sensenova_loop_mlx.py         |  3 +++
 zig/src/families/qwen27/forward.zig |  3 +++
 zig/tests/qwen27/run.zig            | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/sensenova_loop_mlx.py b/tools/sensenova_loop_mlx.py
index 12d60a55c..f639f6948 100644
--- a/tools/sensenova_loop_mlx.py
+++ b/tools/sensenova_loop_mlx.py
@@ -164,6 +164,9 @@ def main():
                 pending[f"{base}.scales"] = torch.from_numpy(s_all.view(np.int16)).view(torch.bfloat16)
                 pending[f"{base}.biases"] = torch.from_numpy(b_all.view(np.int16)).view(torch.bfloat16)
                 checked += 1
+            elif out.endswith("A_log"):
+                # the GDN kernel reads a bf16 decay weight; the checkpoint's A_log is f32
+                pending[out] = t.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous()
             elif out.endswith("dt_bias"):
                 # the engine keeps dt_bias bf16; the checkpoint's is f32
                 pending[out] = t.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous()
